      "math_academy_id": "q-224997",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(X<9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ | $\\,0.7166\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<9) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =F(8) \\\\  & =0.5925.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
